<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Window
    x:Class="PresenterScript.HelpWindow"
    xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
    Title="PresenterScript – Script syntax">
    <Window.SystemBackdrop>
        <MicaBackdrop />
    </Window.SystemBackdrop>

    <Grid>
        <Grid.RowDefinitions>
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />
            <RowDefinition Height="*" />
        </Grid.RowDefinitions>
        <Grid.Resources>
            <Style x:Key="HelpHeading" BasedOn="{StaticResource SubtitleTextBlockStyle}" TargetType="TextBlock">
                <Setter Property="Margin" Value="0,20,0,4" />
            </Style>
            <Style x:Key="HelpBody" BasedOn="{StaticResource BodyTextBlockStyle}" TargetType="TextBlock">
                <Setter Property="TextWrapping" Value="Wrap" />
                <Setter Property="IsTextSelectionEnabled" Value="True" />
            </Style>
            <Style x:Key="HelpCode" TargetType="TextBlock">
                <Setter Property="FontFamily" Value="Cascadia Mono, Consolas" />
                <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="13" />
                <Setter Property="IsTextSelectionEnabled" Value="True" />
                <Setter Property="TextWrapping" Value="Wrap" />
            </Style>
            <Style x:Key="HelpCodeBox" TargetType="Border">
                <Setter Property="Margin" Value="0,8,0,0" />
                <Setter Property="Padding" Value="12,8" />
                <Setter Property="Background" Value="{ThemeResource CardBackgroundFillColorDefaultBrush}" />
                <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{ThemeResource CardStrokeColorDefaultBrush}" />
                <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="1" />
                <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="6" />
            </Style>
        </Grid.Resources>

        <TitleBar x:Name="HelpTitleBar" Title="Script syntax" />

        <ScrollViewer Grid.Row="1" Padding="28,0,28,24">
            <StackPanel MaxWidth="760" Margin="0,8,0,0" HorizontalAlignment="Left">
                <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource HelpBody}">
                    Scripts are ordinary Markdown (headings, emphasis, lists, tables, links, images…). On top of that, PresenterScript understands the following.
                </TextBlock>

                <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource HelpHeading}" Text="Code snippets" />
                <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource HelpBody}">
                    Fenced code blocks are snippets. Click anywhere on a snippet to copy it to the clipboard; its section becomes the current one. Once you paste it somewhere, the highlight moves to the next section and scrolls it to the center. With "Auto-copy next" on, the next snippet is then put on the clipboard automatically. The snippet waiting on the clipboard shows an "On clipboard" badge, which goes away if another app replaces the clipboard.
                </TextBlock>
                <Border Style="{StaticResource HelpCodeBox}">
                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource HelpCode}" xml:space="preserve">```csharp
var app = builder.Build();
```</TextBlock>
                </Border>

                <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource HelpHeading}" Text="Sections" />
                <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource HelpBody}">
                    The prose between snippets forms the sections you step through. The current section is highlighted with a tinted background and larger text. Click a section, or use Up/Down (PageUp/PageDown) in presenter mode, to move between them; Home goes back to the first one.
                </TextBlock>

                <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource HelpHeading}" Text="Section break: ---" />
                <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource HelpBody}">
                    A line with only --- splits the prose into separate sections even when there is no snippet between them. Leave a blank line above it; directly under a line of text, Markdown treats --- as a heading underline instead.
                </TextBlock>
                <Border Style="{StaticResource HelpCodeBox}">
                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource HelpCode}" xml:space="preserve">Talk about the architecture.

---

Now switch to the demo app.</TextBlock>
                </Border>

                <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource HelpHeading}" Text="Time targets: @20" />
                <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource HelpBody}">
                    A line with only @ and a time sets when you should reach that section, measured from the start of the talk: @20 (minutes), @20:30 (minutes:seconds) or @1:05:00 (hours:minutes:seconds). The line itself isn't shown; the section gets a ⏱ badge instead. Tags inside snippets are ignored.
                </TextBlock>
                <Border Style="{StaticResource HelpCodeBox}">
                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource HelpCode}" xml:space="preserve">---
@20:00
Switch to the GitHub Todo app.</TextBlock>
                </Border>
                <TextBlock Margin="0,8,0,0" Style="{StaticResource HelpBody}">
                    You don't need to tag every section. Untagged sections get an estimated target spread evenly between the tagged sections around them: with @10 on one section and @20 three sections later, the two in between are expected at about 13:20 and 16:40. The first section counts as 0:00, and the talk length (below) marks the end, so sections after the last tag are estimated too. Estimated targets aren't shown; they only feed the pace indicator.
                </TextBlock>
                <TextBlock Margin="0,8,0,0" Style="{StaticResource HelpBody}">
                    While presenting, a pill next to the timer shows whether you're ahead of or behind schedule right now. The current section is on schedule from its target until the next section's target (or the end of the talk); before that you're ahead, after it you're behind, and the pill updates every second. A count-down shows "Ready" and hides its pace pill until you first enter presenter mode. Once started, it continues toward the end time even if you return to editing.
                </TextBlock>
                <StackPanel
                    x:Name="PaceLegend"
                    Margin="0,10,0,0"
                    Orientation="Horizontal"
                    Spacing="6" />

                <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource HelpHeading}" Text="Talk length: @30 as the last line" />
                <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource HelpBody}">
                    If the very last line of the script is a time tag, it's the total length of the talk rather than a section target, and an "End of talk" marker is shown. When the timer counts down to an end time, time into the talk is then measured back from the end: with @30 at the end and 5 minutes left, you're 25 minutes in, so a section tagged @25 is right on time. That way it doesn't matter exactly when you switched to presenter mode.
                </TextBlock>
                <TextBlock Margin="0,8,0,0" Style="{StaticResource HelpBody}">
                    Without a count-down (or without a talk length), time into the talk is measured from the talk start time. It's set when you first enter presenter mode and can be changed in the timer menu.
                </TextBlock>

                <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource HelpHeading}" Text="Setup checklist" />
                <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource HelpBody}">
                    A task list at the very top of the script becomes a setup checklist. The heading right above it becomes the checklist's title (otherwise it's titled "Setup"); a talk title above that is fine. It isn't part of the section flow. Click an item to tick it off. In presenter mode it starts collapsed; click its heading to expand it. Ticks last until the app restarts and aren't saved to the file.
                </TextBlock>
                <Border Style="{StaticResource HelpCodeBox}">
                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource HelpCode}" xml:space="preserve"># My Talk

## Setup
- [ ] Turn on Do Not Disturb
- [ ] Display at 125% scale
- [x] Demo repo reset

Welcome everyone…</TextBlock>
                </Border>

                <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource HelpHeading}" Text="Presenter settings" />
                <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource HelpBody}">
                    Open the toolbar's ... menu and choose Presenter settings. Keep system and displays awake is on by default: it prevents idle sleep and display timeout while presenting, including when you switch to another app. The request is released when you return to edit mode or close PresenterScript. Explicit sleep, closing the lid, power policies, and battery limits can still take precedence.
                </TextBlock>
                <TextBlock Margin="0,8,0,0" Style="{StaticResource HelpBody}">
                    Enter full screen automatically is off by default. When enabled, entering presenter mode also enters full screen and leaving restores the previous window mode. If you change the mode yourself with F11, your choice is preserved instead. Save applies these options the next time you enter presenter mode; Cancel discards changes.
                </TextBlock>
                <TextBlock Margin="0,8,0,0" Style="{StaticResource HelpBody}">
                    The dialog shows the current Windows notification mode where supported and links to notification settings so you can turn on Do not disturb manually. Priority notifications or alarms may still appear. It also links to Date &amp; time settings, where newer Windows 11 versions let you turn off "Show time and date in the system tray" to hide the taskbar clock and date. These Windows settings are manual, apply system-wide, and are not changed or restored by PresenterScript.
                </TextBlock>

                <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource HelpHeading}" Text="Keyboard shortcuts" />
                <Grid Margin="0,4,0,0" ColumnSpacing="24" RowSpacing="4">
                    <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                        <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto" />
                        <ColumnDefinition Width="*" />
                    </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                    <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                        <RowDefinition />
                        <RowDefinition />
                        <RowDefinition />
                        <RowDefinition />
                        <RowDefinition />
                        <RowDefinition />
                        <RowDefinition />
                        <RowDefinition />
                    </Grid.RowDefinitions>
                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource HelpCode}" Text="F5 / Esc" />
                    <TextBlock Grid.Column="1" Style="{StaticResource HelpBody}" Text="Presenter mode / back to edit mode" />
                    <TextBlock Grid.Row="7" Style="{StaticResource HelpCode}" Text="F11" />
                    <TextBlock Grid.Row="7" Grid.Column="1" Style="{StaticResource HelpBody}" Text="Full screen" />
                    <TextBlock Grid.Row="1" Style="{StaticResource HelpCode}" Text="Up / Down, PageUp / PageDown" />
                    <TextBlock Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="1" Style="{StaticResource HelpBody}" Text="Previous / next section (presenter mode)" />
                    <TextBlock Grid.Row="2" Style="{StaticResource HelpCode}" Text="Home" />
                    <TextBlock Grid.Row="2" Grid.Column="1" Style="{StaticResource HelpBody}" Text="Back to the first section" />
                    <TextBlock Grid.Row="3" Style="{StaticResource HelpCode}" Text="Ctrl+S / Ctrl+Shift+S" />
                    <TextBlock Grid.Row="3" Grid.Column="1" Style="{StaticResource HelpBody}" Text="Save / Save as" />
                    <TextBlock Grid.Row="4" Style="{StaticResource HelpCode}" Text="Ctrl+O / Ctrl+N" />
                    <TextBlock Grid.Row="4" Grid.Column="1" Style="{StaticResource HelpBody}" Text="Open / New" />
                    <TextBlock Grid.Row="5" Style="{StaticResource HelpCode}" Text="Ctrl+Plus / Ctrl+Minus" />
                    <TextBlock Grid.Row="5" Grid.Column="1" Style="{StaticResource HelpBody}" Text="Zoom the rendered script" />
                    <TextBlock Grid.Row="6" Style="{StaticResource HelpCode}" Text="F1" />
                    <TextBlock Grid.Row="6" Grid.Column="1" Style="{StaticResource HelpBody}" Text="This help" />
                </Grid>

                <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource HelpHeading}" Text="Unsaved changes" />
                <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource HelpBody}">
                    You don't have to save before closing the app. Unsaved edits (marked with • in the title) are kept in scratch space, and the next launch reopens the script with those edits. Use Revert to discard them. Opening or creating another script while there are unsaved changes asks whether to save them first.
                </TextBlock>
            </StackPanel>
        </ScrollViewer>
    </Grid>
</Window>
